  "term": "sympathetic–adrenal–medullary axis",
  "definition": "The sympathetic–adrenal–medullary axis is a body stress-response system described as one of the physiological pathways activated by academic stress. In this packet, it is presented as helping mediate stress-related biological changes, including release of measurable biomarkers such as cortisol.",
